WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
So we're on March 13, 1922 otherwise that will be shot.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:11.000
So the great good on hearing the truth is the beginning of something that will continue on into the higher volumes

3
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.000
and that is the Lord emphasizing the importance of reading and studying the texts

4
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:22.000
and telling us that no matter how much progress you think you have made

5
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.000
that it is very important to keep the study of the texts going.

6
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Okay, so Louisa said I was in my usual state and I found myself in the midst of a flowery valley

7
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.000
in which I found my late confessor who died at the tenth of the current month.

8
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Now is there a note in your book to tell you who that is?

9
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.000
No, it's Father Janaro di Janaro.

10
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
The confessor that she had for years and years in the early stages of the volumes.

11
00:00:52.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Okay, Father Janaro, G-E-N-N-A-R-O, D-Janaro, G-E-N-N-A-R-A-O.

12
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.000
That's a bit like saying Joseph of Joseph.

13
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.000
It's very unusual.

14
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Father Janaro, D-Janaro.

15
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:24.000
And he was her compass for many years and he's going to tell her something

16
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.000
that's actually terribly important.

17
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.000
Now he's now on the other side because he has died.

18
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Okay, so I found my late conference.

19
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.000
She's in and out of the body experience.

20
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.000
According to his habit, when he lived down here, that is in this low place of the earth,

21
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.000
he told me, "Tell me, what did Jesus say to you?"

22
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Because apparently that's what he always said to her, "What did Jesus say to you?"

23
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.000
And Louisa said, "Watch this now.

24
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.000
This is very interesting.

25
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.000
He spoke to me in my interior.

26
00:01:53.000 --> 00:02:01.000
He did not tell me anything with words, and you know that I don't take into account the things I get in my interior."

27
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.000
That's absolutely incredible, isn't it?

28
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Now, what the thing is, that that concurs with the teaching of John on the cross,

29
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.000
not to pay attention to everything you get in your interior.

30
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:17.000
Because it's so hard to find out what you, what's him,

31
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:22.000
and what's a mixture of you, him, and anything else you've read or heard of or whatever.

32
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.000
And she said, "I don't take into account the things I heard in my interior."

33
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:33.000
Now, and the priest said to her, "I want to hear also what he told you in your interior."

34
00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:39.000
Because he had given her the spiritual guidance for years and knew it was Jesus.

35
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Okay.

36
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:46.000
So Louisa said, as though forced, in other words, the priest has asked it,

37
00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:52.000
that Jesus said, "My daughter, I carry you in my arms," because she's in the divine will.

38
00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.000
Okay.

39
00:02:53.000 --> 00:03:01.000
"My arms will serve you as a little boat to let you sail in the interminable sea of my will."

40
00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:07.000
Then, as you do your acts in my will, you will form the sails, the mast,

41
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.000
the anchor, notice they're doing it together.

42
00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.000
Okay.

43
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:16.000
"Which will serve not only as an ornament to the little boat, but to make it move faster.

44
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:25.000
The love I have for one who lives in my will is so great that I carry her in my arms without ever leaving her."

45
00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.000
Isn't that fantastic?

46
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:31.000
And while he was saying this, "I saw the arms of Jesus in the shape of a little boat."

47
00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.000
Now, that would be very interesting to see, wouldn't it?

48
00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.000
And myself in the middle of it.

49
00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.000
Okay.

50
00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:44.000
So Jesus is going to talk to her now about drops of light and understanding.

51
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:48.000
On hearing this, the confessor told me, "You must know."

52
00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.000
And he's teaching her from the other side, which is very, very interesting.

53
00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:59.000
That when Jesus speaks to you and manifests these truths to you, it's like rays of light that drop upon you.

54
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.000
This is where you get the drops.

55
00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.000
Okay.

56
00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.000
Back then, that's when he was on the earth.

57
00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:13.000
When you manifested them to me, not having his virtue that is power, you manifested them drop by drop.

58
00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:17.000
Because Louise is always saying how difficult she finds it to express it.

59
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:22.000
And yet my soul remained all filled with these drops of light.

60
00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:27.000
Now, there's another way of talking about divine will drops of light.

61
00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:35.000
I think it's absolutely magnificent because the divine will is light, and we're only able to take it sip by sip.

62
00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:39.000
That light gave me one, a greater spur.

63
00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:46.000
And two, it gave me more desire to hear the truths, to hear more truths.

64
00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:55.000
In order to be able to receive more light, because the truths being celestial fragrance and divine sensation.

65
00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:58.000
And this was just by hearing them.

66
00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:01.000
What must it have been for Louise to receive it directly?

67
00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:06.000
What then will it be for those who practice them?

68
00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:11.000
Now, there's a huge difference between hearing and putting into practice.

69
00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:19.000
If you go to the letter of St. James, I think it's chapter four.

70
00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:26.000
He says that there's no point in just hearing the word and not going away and putting it into practice.

71
00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:32.000
Because there will be judgment for those who have heard and have done absolutely nothing about it.

72
00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:35.000
But St. James gives it here in a very eloquent way.

73
00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:39.000
So it's in chapter four, it's in most of the chapter four, I think.

74
00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:43.000
So he said, what would it be like for those who actually practice them?

75
00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:48.000
This is why I loved, I desired so much to hear what Jesus told you.

76
00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:52.000
And I wanted to tell others, look at that.

77
00:05:52.000 --> 00:06:00.000
Anyone who has genuinely got divine will wants to share it with others because it's such an incredible treasure.

78
00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.000
You can't keep it to yourself.

79
00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:09.000
It was light and fragrance that I felt and I wanted others to share them.

80
00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:15.000
Now notice, this is at the very beginning, we're only on volume 14 here.

81
00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:24.000
And the priest is saying that he could actually tell others that if nothing else happened to you, you get this wonderful divine fragrance.

82
00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:28.000
Look at the way it can be introduced.

83
00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:33.000
So this light and there's enlightenment in it.

84
00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:37.000
So that's another way of approaching the thing is really interesting.

85
00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:45.000
If you knew the great good that my soul has received in hearing the truths which Jesus was saying to you,

86
00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:51.000
normally in English we would finish that sentence, but in these writings the sentence is never finished.

87
00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:55.000
You know, it would be that you would do something about it or whatever.

88
00:06:55.000 --> 00:07:05.000
How it still drips with light and emanates celestial fragrance, which not only gives me refreshment,

89
00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:09.000
but serves as light to me and to those who are near me.

90
00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:13.000
Where is the priest if he says to those who are near me?

91
00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:16.000
He's in purgatory, yeah.

92
00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:23.000
Okay, because Jesus says in these writings that nine out of ten people go to purgatory, that is the ones who are saved.

93
00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:28.000
He was here.

94
00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:31.000
Well, this is the early days.

95
00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:33.000
This is the early days.

96
00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:37.000
Louisa has only moved into the divine will nobody else has.

97
00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:43.000
And he's guiding her as a priest not knowing where this thing is going.

98
00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:49.000
All he knows is that what Jesus is saying to her is having this effect on him.

99
00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:52.000
And this is before the kingdom of the divine will is established.

100
00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:55.000
We're only on volume 14 out of 36.

101
00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:59.000
Okay, so this is very early days.

102
00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:02.000
Well, I'll finish this and then say something is actually quite important.

103
00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:09.000
But as you do your acts in the divine volition, I take special part in them.

104
00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:14.000
Now, notice the special part because he had been her spiritual guide.

105
00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:19.000
Okay, notice it's in the present tense where he is now.

106
00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:24.000
As you know, the acts affect everybody in heaven, in purgatory and on earth.

107
00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:30.000
Okay, because I feel the seed of his most holy will which you are sowing in me.

108
00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.000
Now, Louisa is not a bit shy talking to people in the body experience.

109
00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:37.000
So she said, okay, show it to me.

110
00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:38.000
How do you drip with light?

111
00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:39.000
I want to see it.

112
00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:41.000
It's really funny.

113
00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:45.000
You couldn't say that to somebody on the earth really, you know.

114
00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.000
Let me see your soul.

115
00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.000
She said, how does it drip with light?

116
00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:53.000
He opened himself at the sight of where the heart is and I saw his soul all dripping with light.

117
00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:57.000
Those drops were emerging and separating, one flowing over the other.

118
00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:58.000
It was beautiful to look at.

119
00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:02.000
And he said, have you seen how beautiful it is to hear the truths?

120
00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:06.000
Those who do not hear them drip with such darkness as to strike terror.

121
00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:08.000
That's coming from the priest now.

122
00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:17.000
Okay, now the bit I want to sort of dialogue with you for a moment is to let you see that

123
00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:25.000
he had been a spiritual director to Louisa and here he is now on the other side telling

124
00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:32.000
Louisa that he was growing and needing the teaching that she was giving to him.

125
00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:34.000
This is the way the Lord does things.

126
00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:37.000
He always works at both ends of the line.

127
00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:43.000
And if you look at the history of the church, we have quite a number of people like this

128
00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:47.000
Catherine of Siena, Father Raymond of Capua.

129
00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:54.000
Now he wasn't canonized, but he was made venerable or beatified.

130
00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:58.000
So while he was directing her, she sanctified him.

131
00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:05.000
Okay, you have Francis of Assisi and Clare of Assisi.

132
00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:10.000
You have Francis de Sales and Jane de Chantal.

133
00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:15.000
You have Teresa Vavala and John of the Cross and there's lots more.

134
00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:19.000
But I want you to see that the Lord is working at both ends of the line.

135
00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:25.000
And when the Lord is making a saint and somebody is trying to guide that person, that person

136
00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:29.000
is way beyond where the guide is.

137
00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:32.000
And so you're automatically pulled up the mountain.

138
00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:33.000
It's absolutely beautiful.

139
00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:38.000
The church has loads of testimony about that.

140
00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:40.000
There are others as well.

141
00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:45.000
There's St. Faustina's at least one priest that guided her as well.

142
00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:47.000
There are others.

143
00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:48.000
Mary and Claude.

144
00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:51.000
Yeah, Claude de la Colombiaire.

145
00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:54.000
That's Margaret Mary Alacoke, isn't it?

146
00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.000
Yeah.

147
00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.000
Okay.

148
00:10:56.000 --> 00:11:00.000
It's just that when you start thinking about it, you realize I hesitate to call them couples

149
00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.000
in case I'd be completely misunderstood.

150
00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:08.000
You know, but there are souls that are coupled together to take this journey.

151
00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:11.000
Now, sometimes the Lord does it differently.

152
00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:18.000
In times of crisis in the church, the Lord often brings forth saints as a bunch of grapes.

153
00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:25.000
Like in the early part of the 20th century, you have Pedro Pio, Maria Valtorta and Louisa

154
00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:28.000
all living close to each other.

155
00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:33.000
And the three saints being brought up together and the Lord revealing himself to all of them,

156
00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:37.000
from different angles, all at the same time.

157
00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:41.000
If you look at St. Therese of Lissue, she came out of a household of saints.

158
00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:45.000
They're all saints, even if they're not all canonized.

159
00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:51.000
And so in the situation that we have in the world today, the Lord is making the divine

160
00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:58.000
will family knit together to protect ourselves from the disaster of the darkness that's out

161
00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:03.000
there so that we can actually go on in the journey of the divine will.

162
00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:05.000
You couldn't do it by yourself.

163
00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:08.000
You wouldn't be strong enough.

164
00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:13.000
Well, some people are, but they're very unusual.

165
00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:14.000
Okay.

166
00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:22.000
So, Marta 16, 1922, to live in the divine will has nothing great externally.

167
00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:24.000
Everything passes between the soul and God.

168
00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:32.000
And this is a very important message that the mission of divine will is interior.

169
00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:36.000
So, no big projects, no big huha.

170
00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:39.000
He's not going to let you work big miracles out there.

171
00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:46.000
And so, you'll do what some of the evangelists do in America run these mega churches and

172
00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:49.000
there's thousands and thousands and you're working miracles.

173
00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:51.000
That's not how divine will works.

174
00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:59.000
Divine will gives you such power to reach people internally that would be a disaster if they

175
00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:01.000
knew you were doing it.

176
00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:02.000
Does that make sense?

177
00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:03.000
Yeah.

178
00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:09.000
And so, he leaves you looking perfectly ordinary to up and tape me on the outside.

179
00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:11.000
That is, if you are up and tape me like me.

180
00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:16.000
And the whole mystery is going on internally, which I absolutely love.

181
00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:21.000
And of course, that was the reality of his mother during her lifetime.

182
00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:23.000
That's what he's going to tell you here.

183
00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:31.000
So, Louisa says, "Continue in my usual state, I was thinking to myself, I feel that I am,

184
00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:36.000
my book says the most bad, which is wonderful English, that I'm the worst of all.

185
00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:41.000
Yet, my sweet Jesus tells me that his designs upon me are great."

186
00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:47.000
So, it seems a contradiction in terms that the work which he is doing in me is so important

187
00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:50.000
that he doesn't want to entrust it even to the angels.

188
00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:54.000
But he himself wants to be the custodian, the actor, and the spectator.

189
00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:57.000
Yet, what great things do I do?

190
00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:58.000
Nothing.

191
00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:05.000
My exterior, my exterior life is so ordinary that I do nothing beneath others.

192
00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:06.000
Okay?

193
00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:10.000
I do things beneath others, which is very poor English.

194
00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:12.000
In other words, I...

195
00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:14.000
Less than?

196
00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:15.000
Less than.

197
00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:16.000
Yeah.

198
00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:18.000
Because what she did was crochet.

199
00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:19.000
Do you know what I mean?

200
00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:23.000
She didn't make the dinner, she didn't clean the house, she didn't visit the neighbours,

201
00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:27.000
she didn't visit the old and the sick, she didn't do anything outside.

202
00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:30.000
So, it seems as if she was doing absolutely nothing.

203
00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:31.000
Yeah.

204
00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:37.000
So, while I was thinking of this, my beloved Jesus, cutting off my thoughts, sometimes

205
00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:40.000
he did because he couldn't take any more.

206
00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:47.000
He told me, "My daughter, it shows how without your Jesus you can think, I'd say nothing,

207
00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:48.000
but nonsense.

208
00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:49.000
Okay?

209
00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:50.000
I loved."

210
00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:52.000
That's John 15.5.

211
00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:56.000
Without me, you can do nothing good understood.

212
00:14:56.000 --> 00:15:01.000
And Philippians 4.13, but with him I can do everything.

213
00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:07.000
My dear mother, sorry I don't do the memo, but that's far too Italian for me.

214
00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:13.000
My dear mother also did nothing extraordinary in her exterior life.

215
00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:16.000
Even more, apparently, she did less than others.

216
00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:22.000
And that's what Luz was trying to say up there, "I appear to do less than others."

217
00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:26.000
She lowered herself to the most ordinary actions of life.

218
00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:30.000
She would spin, sew, sweep, light the fire, it seems to everybody else.

219
00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:33.000
Who would ever have thought that she was the mother of God?

220
00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:35.000
You can't say "Ah, God" in English.

221
00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:41.000
You can't say that in rehearsal because in English that would presume other gods.

222
00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:48.000
But that's a transliteration of Italian in which the "Ah" is required in the Italian,

223
00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:50.000
but not in English.

224
00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:54.000
Her external actions indicated nothing of this.

225
00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:58.000
And when she carried me in her womb containing the eternal word within herself,

226
00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:05.000
every motion of hers, every human action won the adoration of the whole of creation.

227
00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:10.000
Okay, that's your Romans 8.19.

228
00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:15.000
That the whole of creation was waiting for this daughter of God to turn up.

229
00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:20.000
That would start the whole redemption and therefore the kingdom of the divine will afterwards.

230
00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:24.000
From her came the life and the preservation of all creatures,

